sentences.l:
Look at the garden, the fresh-one: as if * there were spread over it a sheet, green;
if ever you turn with the glance of your eye, you will not see * except a pool in which the water roams;
and you see in yourself a might in its great-trees, * since above your head, wherever you go, is a banner.

sentences.i:
Look at the fresh green garden: it is as though * a green cloak had been spread over it;
wherever your glance turns you see nothing * but a pool where the water wanders;
and you feel a pride within you among its tall trees, * for wherever you walk a banner waves above your head.
